Subject: [PATCH net-next v1 6/6] Documentation: networking: document the
 UDP-tunnel inner-flow descents

Add the "Tunnel inner-flow descent" section to the flow dissector
overview: why the dissector keeps the outer tuple for UDP tunnels by
default, what the *_inner gates change (skb->hash reflects the inner
flow), why the descents are off by default and never auto-managed,
and the byte-identical fast==slow property that makes enabling one a
policy choice rather than a path choice.

The per-knob reference for the descent gates lives in
Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst, added by the per-tunnel
patches; this overview links to it.

